            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": ". Skeuomorphism has its roots in the field of industrial design, where it has longly been used to make new products feel more familiar and comfortable to users. Today Skeuomorphism is commonly used in user interface (UI) and webdesign, but also in architecture, ceramics, industrial design and interior design. In the Web Skeuomorphism was largely replaced by ",
